{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness","id":1088050,"title":"Monte Cook's World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-04T19:15:21-07:00","id":1088050,"title":"Monte Cook's World of Darkness?","content":"So I've been interested in checking out Monte Cook's World of Darkness game, which I am lead to believe was either heavily inspired by World of Darkness, or is an alternate portrayal of the same game. I'm not completely sure, because there are far, far fewer videos out there explaining this game than there are for the White Wolf version.<br /> <br /> If anybody around here has checked out the game in more detail, I'd like to know if the game is worth picking up; or if its lack of attention is a sign of what I can expect. I know the gist of the story, being that a crap load of supernatural shit invaded the world just over a year ago, but beyond that, I don't have anything to go on. Just that it's a semi-post apocalyptic scenario with vampires, mages, demons, werewolves, and awakened hoomans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:38:54-07:00","id":1088061,"title":"","content":"I've never returned a book for a refund until I purchased Mr. Cooks World of darkness. It's another one of his interesting setting horrible mechanic's games (play a spell caster, win the world) only the setting isn't really that interesting.<br /> <br /> Also all the material is from New world of darkness/chronicles of darkness, so you might get better results in that section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-04-2017, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:49:26-07:00","id":1088064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088061#post1088061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never returned a book for a refund until I purchased Mr. Cooks World of darkness. It's another one of his interesting setting horrible mechanic's games (play a spell caster, win the world) only the setting isn't really that interesting.<br /> <br /> Also all the material is from New world of darkness/chronicles of darkness, so you might get better results in that section.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've found maybe 2 videos on youtube reviewing the game, and they say that the mechanics are somewhat like those of D&amp;D, in the sense of having a level up progression system and <b>'point based magic,'</b> which I'm unclear what that means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:50:17-07:00","id":1088065,"title":"","content":"From what I can remember it's a very clunky D20 system. By point based it gives you X number spell points per level and each spell costs X points to cast. So it's not like regular d&amp;d where you get X spells per a level per day to cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T23:04:54-07:00","id":1088117,"title":"","content":"It's so fucking bad, dude. It's so fucking bad.<br /> <br /> Imagine d20 RIFTS and you're most of the way there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T23:20:06-07:00","id":1088123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088117#post1088117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine d20 RIFTS and you're most of the way there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Werewolves and vampires are aliens. Not sure why the even bothered to call it 'World of Darkness' at all, shit has almost nothing in common with the WoD.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T00:15:39-07:00","id":1088130,"title":"","content":"I have a project that aims to consider each and every book of both the oWod and the nWoD, from the good to the bad to the 'burn this hate crime'/'who would write this' end of the spectrum. <i>Even I won't touch the MCWoD with a ten foot pole.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T00:24:22-07:00","id":1088133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088123#post1088123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Werewolves and vampires are aliens. Not sure why the even bothered to call it 'World of Darkness' at all, shit has almost nothing in common with the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the names and mechanics language is the same, if he tried to sell it as something separate it would probably have only sold slightly better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:08:49-07:00","id":1088186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088123#post1088123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Werewolves and vampires are aliens. Not sure why the even bothered to call it 'World of Darkness' at all, shit has almost nothing in common with the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, the reviewers say they're spirits who are possessing human bodies. And the preview of the game on DriveThru seems to indicate that the 'good monsters' are faced with internal conflict as the spirit and host battle for control of the body. So really, not any different from what Vampires and Werewolves are already dealing with in White Wolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the fact this thing doesn't even have a wiki (as far as I can tell), means that if I want any actual information about this book, I need to pick it up myself. Nobody else seems willing to go into a more in depth explanation about the world and systems beyond generalization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088065#post1088065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can remember it's a very clunky D20 system. By point based it gives you X number spell points per level and each spell costs X points to cast. So it's not like regular d&amp;d where you get X spells per a level per day to cast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, so it's video game format, then? That's new, haven't heard of that in table top, before.<br /> <br /> As for the dice, I have a heck of a lot more D20's laying around than I do D10's. In fact, I think I've got <i>maybe two</i> 10 sided dice total, which makes rolling for Chronicles of Darkness rather complicated, as you can imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-05-2017, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:14:31-07:00","id":1088188,"title":"","content":"that's because it's hot garbage, wanna find out how bad? buy it, don't say we didn't warn you....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:27:45-07:00","id":1088195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088188#post1088188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that's because it's hot garbage, wanna find out how bad? buy it, don't say we didn't warn you....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So everybody seems to be telling me that the setting is fine, but the mechanics are bad. Is that, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Monte_Cook%27s_World_of_Darkness_Rulebook\" target=\"_blank\">Also, found a wiki</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:35:22-07:00","id":1088199,"title":"","content":"The setting is garbage too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:39:08-07:00","id":1088200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088195#post1088195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So everybody seems to be telling me that the setting is fine, but the mechanics are bad. Is that, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Monte_Cook%27s_World_of_Darkness_Rulebook\" target=\"_blank\">Also, found a wiki</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The Mechanics are d20 based. Do you like d20? Then they're mostly fine. Do you dislike d20? Then they're not fine.<br /> <br /> As for the setting, <i>that</i> is why I don't want to go read it again - I regularly read books from gamelines that have mechanics that I would never actually play with. It's a bad setting in general, and worse for slapping the WoD label on to try and spin a buck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:48:00-07:00","id":1088202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088200#post1088200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Mechanics are d20 based. Do you like d20? Then they're mostly fine. Do you dislike d20? Then they're not fine.<br /> <br /> As for the setting, <i>that</i> is why I don't want to go read it again - I regularly read books from gamelines that have mechanics that I would never actually play with. It's a bad setting in general, and worse for slapping the WoD label on to try and spin a buck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't mind D20's. Heck, I was aware of D&amp;D long before I even heard of World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if the mechanics are decent, then what's wrong with the setting? Because the idea I'm getting is that the monsters in Monte Cook have decided not to take the clean and quiet approach and are actively trying to ruin the world. Something which I could see being a nice break away from White Wolf's setting. In fact, that's probably how a lot of role playing settings portray the monsters as being villains. But World of Darkness was the first game I came across where being able to play as the monster was part of the mainstream element, instead of a side option like it was in D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:16:20-07:00","id":1088213,"title":"","content":"The setting overall is a clumsy, chaotic hodgepodge of muddled ideas that don't play nicely together and which throws in names from the WoD randomly and with no relation whatsoever to their 'proper' use. It's like Monte couldn't decide between creating a WoD game, a variant of Dark Matter, and a game based around spirit possession, so he did all three at once, and it suffers from it heavily.<br /> <br /> Also, 'the setting is d20 based' is not 'it uses d20s'. It specifically means it uses the D20 system from WotC. It's a much less generic statement and really says it all - if you like those mechanics, they're fine, and if not, they're not great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:50:30-07:00","id":1088225,"title":"","content":"The basic setting- the Iconnu (generic eldritch abominations) have punched through into our world to destroy it. While they did a lot of damage and turned a decent chuck of the USA into a chaotic nightmare realm, they weren't able to actually destroy the world because it supported by people called the awakened (no relation to nwod Mages, they're just kind of...cool people?), so the Iconnu sent spirits to kill them all. Vampires are humans possessed by the damned, werewolves are possessed by spirits of rage, and demons are spirits possessing inanimate objects. So it is up to you to save the awakened (or kill them all I guess if you want to play the bad guys).<br /> <br /> The supernatural is hidden although I'm not sure how because in Chicago the streets are eating people.<br /> <br /> Also there are mages because this is nominally a world of darkness game. They're kind of shoehorned in. They don't really do much.<br /> <br /> It's got a lot of the names from the nwod but not much actual connection, it's basically D&amp;D. Each monster is a class, the rules are otherwise the same. As loomer said, if you like that great, if not you won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:34:32-07:00","id":1088253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088225#post1088225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic setting- the Iconnu (generic eldritch abominations) have punched through into our world to destroy it. While they did a lot of damage and turned a decent chuck of the USA into a chaotic nightmare realm, they weren't able to actually destroy the world because it supported by people called the awakened (no relation to nwod Mages, they're just kind of...cool people?), so the Iconnu sent spirits to kill them all. Vampires are humans possessed by the damned, werewolves are possessed by spirits of rage, and demons are spirits possessing inanimate objects. So it is up to you to save the awakened (or kill them all I guess if you want to play the bad guys).<br /> <br /> The supernatural is hidden although I'm not sure how because in Chicago the streets are eating people.<br /> <br /> Also there are mages because this is nominally a world of darkness game. They're kind of shoehorned in. They don't really do much.<br /> <br /> It's got a lot of the names from the nwod but not much actual connection, it's basically D&amp;D. Each monster is a class, the rules are otherwise the same. As loomer said, if you like that great, if not you won't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hmmm, well I think I'll give it a check out eventually. It's price tag is about 30 to 40 bucks cheaper than the other World of Darkness games, which is a nice bonus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:04:14-07:00","id":1088265,"title":"","content":"The OP was asking for info, repeated telling him the game sucks doesn't really help him. It was never designed to be the d20 version of our WoD, but specifically like the tin says: Monte Cook's version of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:21:27-07:00","id":1088274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088253#post1088253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmm, well I think I'll give it a check out eventually. It's price tag is about 30 to 40 bucks cheaper than the other World of Darkness games, which is a nice bonus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Believe me, it's not worth it despite being cheaper. There's a very good reason why as you pointed out, no one talks about Monte Cook's World of Darkness. It's a <b><i>terrible</i> </b>book and not worth getting unless you're some kind of WoD/CofD or Monte Cook completionist. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12109\" data-vbnamecard=\"12109\">Urbenmyth</a>'s comment about the setting is pretty much all you get for the setting and as they and others pointed out, it's a God-awful mess of a setting that's paper thin.<br /> <br /> If you want something good from Monte Cook, get Numenera.<br /> <br /> If you want something good in a post world changing supernatural event setting, get Shadowrun.<br /> <br /> If you want something good from the WoD or CofD, get <i>any</i> WoD/CofD rulebook.<br /> <br /> Because while Monte Cook has done some great work for RPGs, his World of Darkness is not one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:29:28-07:00","id":1088275,"title":"","content":"Before you put money down, especially if it's limited, have a read here. <a href=\"http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal-and-friends/piell/monte-cooks-world-of-darkness/\" target=\"_blank\">http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal...d-of-darkness/</a> It's a Fatal and Friends review of the game, and while FnF tends to be a little critical (it is, afterall, mostly a thread series about 'what the hell is this' and 'who designed this mechanic' that spawned out of a hate-read of FATAL), it covers most of our objections. Well, some of them, the read got abandoned halfway through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:17:12-07:00","id":1088296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088202#post1088202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if the mechanics are decent, then what's wrong with the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, the biggest problem people have that it was labelled as WoD and it's not and this is a WoD forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally, I'm okay with d20 too, although I like the storyteller system better. The setting of the game is an interesting one, I don't think it's worse than a lot of other rpgs, it's just not WoD.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:39:16-07:00","id":1088338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088274#post1088274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Believe me, it's not worth it despite being cheaper. There's a very good reason why as you pointed out, no one talks about Monte Cook's World of Darkness. It's a <b><i>terrible</i> </b>book and not worth getting unless you're some kind of WoD/CofD or Monte Cook completionist.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12109\" data-vbnamecard=\"12109\">Urbenmyth</a>'s comment about the setting is pretty much all you get for the setting and as they and others pointed out, it's a God-awful mess of a setting that's paper thin.<br /> <br /> If you want something good from Monte Cook, get Numenera.<br /> <br /> If you want something good in a post world changing supernatural event setting, get Shadowrun.<br /> <br /> If you want something good from the WoD or CofD, get <i>any</i> WoD/CofD rulebook.<br /> <br /> Because while Monte Cook has done some great work for RPGs, his World of Darkness is not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've actually been very interested to check out Shadowrun and 5th edition D&amp;D, but I can't seem to locate their respective books. That, or they're going by completely different titles and I don't know what I'm supposed to be searching for.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm saving up for Changeling: the Lost 2e when it finally comes out. That's the next book I had planned on getting for the Chronicles of Darkness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:53:12-07:00","id":1088344,"title":"","content":"You have to buy D&amp;D 5E in an actual store. Any Barnes and Noble will do. Not sure about Shadowrun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our society is held together by the thinnest of threads: that exquisitely refined sense of tribal order.<br /> Edith Wharton, The Age of Innocence<br /> <br /> I am a huge fan of both the Trinity Universe and the classic World of Darkness.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12799-spellfire22","name":"Spellfire22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:25:01-07:00","id":1088362,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spellfire22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088344#post1088344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to buy D&amp;D 5E in an actual store. Any Barnes and Noble will do. Not sure about Shadowrun.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't live near a Barnes and Noble, not since I moved up to a quiet little mountain town. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088275#post1088275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before you put money down, especially if it's limited, have a read here. <a href=\"http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal-and-friends/piell/monte-cooks-world-of-darkness/\" target=\"_blank\">http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal...d-of-darkness/</a> It's a Fatal and Friends review of the game, and while FnF tends to be a little critical (it is, afterall, mostly a thread series about 'what the hell is this' and 'who designed this mechanic' that spawned out of a hate-read of FATAL), it covers most of our objections. Well, some of them, the read got abandoned halfway through.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> THANK YOU! This helps immensely!<br /> <br /> <br /> Although, I've got to say that even though this review seems like it's trying to portray the game in a negative light, I'm actually finding the stuff quite appealing. It's making me want to check it out even more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:26:02-07:00","id":1088365,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/2216/Catalyst-Game-Labs?src=browse2216\" target=\"_blank\">DriveThruRPG </a>has Shadowrun in all its Editions. And of course Shadowrun's publisher, <a href=\"https://store.catalystgamelabs.com/collections/shadowrun\" target=\"_blank\">Catalyst Game Labs</a>, has the current Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:22:10-07:00","id":1088416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, I've got to say that even though this review seems like it's trying to portray the game in a negative light, I'm actually finding the stuff quite appealing. It's making me want to check it out even more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then go for it...<br /> <br /> I don't know anythting about it, but want to tell a funny anecdote: A friend of mine told me that he played that game once, and he generated his character with a random system that the game has. He ended with a young kid...that knew how to drive tanks, elicopters, and use heavy weapons (but not small ones).<br /> Needless to say, my frined found the game to be quite a trip <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:05:46-07:00","id":1088507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088416#post1088416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then go for it...<br /> <br /> I don't know anythting about it, but want to tell a funny anecdote: A friend of mine told me that he played that game once, and he generated his character with a random system that the game has. He ended with a young kid...that knew how to drive tanks, elicopters, and use heavy weapons (but not small ones).<br /> Needless to say, my frined found the game to be quite a trip <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;And how did you learn to do all this, little boy?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;uhh... Nightmare Wave?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Alright then, welcome to the team!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> Though when I wrote my last post, I hadn't yet gotten to the review on the class mechanics. Playing a Demon sounds like it would be a horrendous grind fest or a horrendous resource management. They're practically compelled to be the mastermind of the group. But the premise of playing characters who don't necessarily care about morality and maintaining their human lives is still interesting. It sounds a bit like Beast's original write up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-05-2017, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:11:45-07:00","id":1088509,"title":"","content":"Setting: You could call it... I don't know, from nWoD terminoly, a &quot;shard&quot; setting. You might like shards, you might not like shards.<br /> Mechanics: The mechanics aren't that bad, it's basically each splat is a class to use on the d20 class based system instead of ST's freeform. If you just like playing d20 (and I gotta say I enjoy more d20 than ST) and wants to play those classes, it works.<br /> <br /> I think the real problem with the book is that it tried to bring <b>two</b> new things to a gameline that has a very specific fanbase. Both another setting and a new system. If they tried only one of them, it could've worked.<br /> <br /> <b>Another setting:</b> IMHO, if the book presented itself as a ST supplement, using ST rules, but using this shard-like setting with some new rules and such, it could work. <b>Public:</b> Something like this could attract WoD and ST fans interested on alternate settings for their system. The setting is no Ptolus or Numenera, but... could've been.<br /> <br /> <b>Another system:</b> It also would work if it presented itself as a real d20 conversion of WoD, if the classes and powers worked closer to the original. I think it would actually be pretty neat if, for example, the vampire class had clans or bloodlines as its archetypes that the player picks one, and its powers were basically disciplines converted (and maybe even streamlined) to a d20 format. If memory serves me right there was a <a href=\"http://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/VampireTheMasquerade/\" target=\"_blank\">GURPS: Vampire the Masquerade</a> book a long while ago, it did its best to convert the template and powers exactly as they worked on the WoD setting, instead of creating a whole new vampire that mechanically didn't work like the original. That kind of conversion might pick up the interest of people that enjoy a setting but not the system, and can't (or don't think its possible) to separate setting from rules. I'm pretty sure the GURPS folks from the time enjoyed it. <b>Public:</b> Something like this could've attracted the D&amp;D and d20 crowd looking to know the real WoD setting that they heard those goth kids talking about. Maybe they could play that cool vampire setting with the green books, while using their favorite d20! Instead what they got was a... generic monsters setting...<br /> <br /> I've done my own conversion of CotD to the AGE system that I love, and these days I play all kinds of WoD using only the AGE rules. Will ST fans be interested? Probably not. AGE fans? Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:22:36-07:00","id":1088515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088117#post1088117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine d20 RIFTS and you're most of the way there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's GAMMA WORLD + URBAN ARCANA, which would actually be kind of awesome. <br /> <br /> MCWOD was mostly a marketing stunt. Cooke was at the time really famous in d20 circles for his long time work on D&amp;D and his own OGL material, so anything with his name on it was likely to attract customers from among his fans. Likewise, WoD was a big brand name with a sizable fan base. So the idea of [Brand Name Person] doing his interpretation of [Brand Name Setting] was guaranteed to sell if just on curiosity alone. However, I can't really give an opinion on the final product. I skimmed some of it at the store and decided it wasn't really for me at the time. But it may be something worth checking out if you think it sounds interesting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:34:06-07:00","id":1088522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088416#post1088416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then go for it...<br /> <br /> I don't know anythting about it, but want to tell a funny anecdote: A friend of mine told me that he played that game once, and he generated his character with a random system that the game has. He ended with a young kid...that knew how to drive tanks, elicopters, and use heavy weapons (but not small ones).<br /> Needless to say, my frined found the game to be quite a trip <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That actually sounds like a fun creative exercise. &quot;Here, roll up a totally random character, then try to justify it in the setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Palladium's NightSPAWN - no, I will not call it Nightbane, no matter how much Mr. McFarlane may complain - was really fun for that. Where else would a skinless gorilla with a TV for a head and chainsaw for an arm be considered perfectly normal?)<br /> <br /> ((And my favorite anecdote is still that, in Rifts, you can apparently play a humpback whale who knows how to flyfish.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T19:42:40-07:00","id":1089535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spellfire22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088344#post1088344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about Shadowrun.</div> </div> </div> </div>DriveThru seems to be selling Shadowrun stuff, but not the core rule book, or at least not that I've been able to find. Looking for fifth edition only brings up previews, or PDF's which 'correct some mistakes' the core book had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T09:19:43-07:00","id":1090335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1089535#post1089535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DriveThru seems to be selling Shadowrun stuff, but not the core rule book, or at least not that I've been able to find. Looking for fifth edition only brings up previews, or PDF's which 'correct some mistakes' the core book had.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? The <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/115985/Shadowrun-Fifth-Edition-Core-Rulebook-Master-Index-Edition?cPath=4328_10253\" target=\"_blank\">5E Rulebook</a> is there. In fact when you go to the Shadowrun 5E page in the Catalyst Game Labs section, it's right at the top of the list of book as DriveThruRPG often does, arranging the corebook at the top of the book list.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:37:39-07:00","id":1090436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1090335#post1090335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you talking about? The <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/115985/Shadowrun-Fifth-Edition-Core-Rulebook-Master-Index-Edition?cPath=4328_10253\" target=\"_blank\">5E Rulebook</a> is there. In fact when you go to the Shadowrun 5E page in the Catalyst Game Labs section, it's right at the top of the list of book as DriveThruRPG often does, arranging the corebook at the top of the book list.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's just a PDF, I prefer a hard cover book. Also, I didn't know that was the book, I thought it was some kind of editorial update or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:55:11-07:00","id":1090445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1090436#post1090436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just a PDF, I prefer a hard cover book. Also, I didn't know that was the book, I thought it was some kind of editorial update or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>...yeah, for whatever reason, CGL made the decision to not allow for ordering physical books of their stuff on DRPG. You'd have to go directly to their store page if you want a hard copy:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://store.catalystgamelabs.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://store.catalystgamelabs.com/cdn/shop/files/logo.png?v=1727694914\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.catalystgamelabs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Catalyst Game Labs Store </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.catalystgamelabs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://store.catalystgamelabs.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The official store for games such as BattleTech, Shadowrun, Dragonfire, Leviathans, Valiant Universe, Cosmic Patrol as well as other card, dice, and tabletop games. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:03:37-07:00","id":1090447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1090436#post1090436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's just a PDF, I prefer a hard cover book. Also, I didn't know that was the book, I thought it was some kind of editorial update or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is technically an updated version in that it includes a Master Index of the 5E hence the Master Index Edition attached to the title. As it says in the blurb.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a physical book, go to the Catalyst Game Labs store site as I mentioned and linked in a previous post. They sell both digital and physical books. The Core Rule book is <a href=\"https://store.catalystgamelabs.com/collections/shadowrun/products/shadowrun-fifth-edition-core-rulebook-master-index-edition?variant=26847236809\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. However the physical book is quite pricey, even on Amazon. Which is understandable as the industry has pretty much moved to PDFs and Print on Demand. You might find it cheaper in a store or secondhand but honestly you could get on PDF along with several other books for the same price as the physical book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T20:10:32-07:00","id":1093075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088050-monte-cook-s-world-of-darkness?p=1088225#post1088225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic setting- the Iconnu (generic eldritch abominations) have punched through into our world to destroy it. While they did a lot of damage and turned a decent chuck of the USA into a chaotic nightmare realm, they weren't able to actually destroy the world because it supported by people called the awakened (no relation to nwod Mages, they're just kind of...cool people?), so the Iconnu sent spirits to kill them all. Vampires are humans possessed by the damned, werewolves are possessed by spirits of rage, and demons are spirits possessing inanimate objects. So it is up to you to save the awakened (or kill them all I guess if you want to play the bad guys).<br /> <br /> The supernatural is hidden although I'm not sure how because in Chicago the streets are eating people.<br /> <br /> Also there are mages because this is nominally a world of darkness game. They're kind of shoehorned in. They don't really do much.<br /> <br /> It's got a lot of the names from the nwod but not much actual connection, it's basically D&amp;D. Each monster is a class, the rules are otherwise the same. As loomer said, if you like that great, if not you won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Awakened are essentially a transplant of <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b>'s protagonists: ordinary humans empowered by a cosmic force to oppose monsters.<br /> <br /> Mages? I employ a small hack for them, which I'll get to shortly. As written, they're an adaptation of ChroD's mages, with their five-fold divide exactly mirroring <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s Paths. In MtAw, the protagonists draw their power from a \u201cSupernal World\u201d encompassing five Realms (one per Path) that act as a sort of \u201csource code\u201d for reality. If I recall correctly, MCWoD doesn't get into any of that; it just says \u201cspellcasters, classified into five types\u201d. <br /> <br /> My hack? I say that MCWoD's mages draw their sorcery from the nightmare realms whence the setting's eldritch abominations came. Picture dark, twisted, and corrupt versions of MtAw's Supernal Realms, sort of like MtAw's Abyssal Watchtowers: these are the homelands of the Iconnu(sp?), and mages are people who have stolen power from these realms. <br /> <br /> Not that I've actually played the game; D&amp;D isn't really my thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T00:38:59-07:00","id":1103744,"title":"","content":"Dangit, and I was actually pretty happy to find this game on the shelf of a gaming and collectables store I've seen around. Now that I've read some more (after I bought it to boot), I'm not nearly so much. Probably paid far more than I should have for the book, though given it's a hardcover I shouldn't be too surprised.<br /> <br /> Eh, I'll chock it to a learning experience or something. Probably won't get the chance to play the game, but...eh. Shoulda done more research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T01:27:37-07:00","id":1103750,"title":"","content":"I don't know, you might still be able to use some elements from the game. Sometimes players get a little too complacent about the World of Darkness, since they know so much about the setting already. it might be fun to borrow a little of this game's weirdness to shake things up a bit. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T11:22:42-07:00","id":1103865,"title":"","content":"I found it fairly cheap and picked it up just to add to my collection. I've been able to use a section here of there to add WoD-ish creatures to my ongoing DnD game. So it isn't a complete loss for me. As a standalone game though, the book was very disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}